    "icon": "data:image/png;base64,",
    "description": "Finds which polygon (territory, zone, area) each latitude / longitude point falls in, from GeoJSON or WKT shapes, and counts points per polygon.",
    "category": "Analytics",
    "subcategory": "Geo",
    "tags": [
        "point in polygon",
        "spatial join",
        "geojson",
        "wkt",
        "territory",
        "geo",
        "visokio-agents"
    ],
    "introductoryText": "Tags each point (customer, property, incident, vehicle position) with the **area it falls in**: sales territory, delivery zone, council or ward, flood zone, catchment. The areas are polygons, one per row of the second input, with the shape in a text field:\n\n- **GeoJSON** geometry (`Polygon`, `MultiPolygon`, or a `Feature`), as exported by most GIS tools and open-data portals\n- **WKT** (`POLYGON ((lon lat, ...))`, `MULTIPOLYGON`), as stored in many databases\n\nHoles are respected (a region *outside* a city, for example), and points on overlapping polygons can return the first match or all matches. Every polygon's other fields are appended to its points (prefixed *Polygon:*), and the second output counts the points (and sums a value) per polygon, with a note for any geometry that could not be read.\n\nCoordinates are longitude / latitude in decimal degrees (WGS84). Pure numpy: no GIS libraries to install.",
    "dependencies": "",
